     "text": "Woodard LLC Clinic\n\nRe: Gwendolyn Orozco (DOB 10/22/1965)\n\n---\n\nAugust 12, 2025\n\nThis letter pertains to Ms. Gwendolyn Orozco, who was seen today regarding her ongoing management of breast cancer, stage II. During her visit, her blood pressure was recorded at 141/89, and her weight was 156 pounds. Ms. Orozco is currently on letrozole 2.5 mg, which has effective in managing her condition. Her cancer has been in a controlled state following treatment approximately 2.3 years ago.\n\n---\n\nNovember 17, 2024\n\nMs. Orozco was seen today for a follow-up regarding her breast cancer, stage II. Her blood pressure at the time was 154/95, and she weighed 159 pounds. She continues to do well without any new complications or recurrence of her cancer. \n\n---\n\nFebruary 23, 2024\n\nMs. Orozco visited on this date for a rash. Her blood pressure was 153/93, and her was 155 pounds. She has a history of breast cancer, stage II, which has been managed effectively following treatment approximately 2.3 years ago. The rash was evaluated and treated 30, 2023\n\nMs. Orozco came in today for a flu shot. Her blood pressure was 149/84, and she weighed 168 pounds. She is doing well overall, with no significant issues reported. Her breast cancer, stage II, remains controlled.\n\n---\n\nSeptember 04, 2022\n\nMs. Orozco was seen today regarding her breast cancer, stage II. At the time, her blood pressure was 139/88, and she weighed 164 pounds. She is doing with her ongoing treatment and has been in a controlled state since her initial treatment approximately 2.3 years ago.\n\n---\n\nDecember 09, 2021\n\nMs. Orozco visited today regarding her breast cancer, stage II. Her blood pressure was 154/91, and she weighed 162 pounds. She has a history of breast cancer, stage II, which has been successfully managed following treatment approximately 2.3 years ago. Ms. Orozco continues to do well.\n\n---\n\n**Additional Information:**\n\nMs. Orozco engages in regular physical activity, running 3-4 times per week. Her social history includes a past use of tobacco, specifically cigarettes, at a rate of one per day, which she quit in September 2022. She has minimized the disclosure of this habit. Ms. Orozco also consumes alcohol approximately three times per week. There is a family history of hypertension in her mother, who was at the age of 77 and passed away at 91.\n\n---\n\nDr. Megan Watson\nWoodard LLC Clinic\nOncology Specialist\n\n---\n\nPlease feel free to contact me if you require any further information.\n\nSincerely,\n\nDr. Megan Watson\n"
